<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cairo Conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> Conference was a meeting held in Cairo in November 1943 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franklin-d-roosevelt">Franklin D. Roosevelt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a> to plan the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Its Cairo Declaration stated that Japan would be stripped of the Pacific islands it had seized and that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penghu">Pescadores</a> would be restored to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It marked the Republic of China's recognition as one of the major Allied powers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cairo-conference.jpg" alt="Cairo Conference" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roosevelt, Franklin D. (Franklin Delano) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cairo_conference.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
